# s08 -- REPEATABLE READ: a row lock over a sealed tombstone is
# judged by the version under it.
#
# S seals R1, unchanged since T1's snapshot: T1's exclusive lock on
# it is granted, as FOR UPDATE of a row the seal moved must be
# (COLSTORE.md §9.1). T2 updates R2 after T1 began, then S seals
# it: T1's lock on R2 is a conflict, as over the update itself.


== pairing RR/RR == T1=RR T2=RC S=RC
@1 T1 begin -> ok
@2 T1 read R1 -> 0
@3 S begin -> ok
@4 S seal R1 -> ok
@5 S commit -> ok
@6 T1 lock R1 exclusive -> ok
@6 check last T1 ok -> satisfied
@7 T2 begin -> ok
@8 T2 write R2 1 -> ok
@9 T2 commit -> ok
@10 S begin -> ok
@11 S seal R2 -> ok
@12 S commit -> ok
@13 T1 lock R2 exclusive -> conflict
@13 check last T1 conflict -> satisfied
@14 check committed T2 S -> satisfied
